  "worked_solution": "First, we calculate $P(A\\cup B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\  & =0.4+0.5-0.2 \\\\  & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A\\cap {B}^{\u2032}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041480/assets/52a7c0ed9285d2699087f0ef817257eacebfabd5cfb2117167730a66b94da3e6.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cap {B}^{\u2032})=0.2.\n$$",
